// ADR-038 D7, question 2, first rule - the other side of it.
//
// Identical to `../crossing` except for the name of the function called, which
// is the same crossing through a foreign API whose author wrote
// `unsafe impl Send` for a type that is not. **This one builds and runs**, and
// increments an `Rc` refcount on a thread the foreign runtime owns - the
// foreign crate's `Rc`, not one this language wrote. `Shared` is an atomic
// count at both settings since ADR-037 D6, and ADR-061 D1 refuses one handed
// to code nothing describes, so a Nikaia value cannot be smuggled this way:
// what is smuggled here came from the other side of the boundary.
//
// Nikaia contributes nothing to either outcome. That is the measurement.
fn main() {
    let handle = hyper_shim::local_handle("not Send".to_string())
    let crossed = hyper_shim::across_a_thread_unchecked(handle)
    println(f"crossed: {crossed}")
}
